ryoute no naka tashikamete

00:01:44.310 --> 00:01:57.070
The time that meets the new morning
atarashii asa ni deau toki ga ugakidasuyo

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:07.860
Kawasumi-san.

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:11.360
I have something to talk about. Please come with us.

00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:16.410
I'm asking...

00:02:16.530 --> 00:02:19.320
Where's the proof that she broke the glass!?

00:02:19.370 --> 00:02:20.160
There isn't any.

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:21.450
In that case...!

00:02:21.700 --> 00:02:24.370
But, there isn't any proof that she didn't do it.

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:26.210
What do you mean by that?

00:02:26.920 --> 00:02:28.630
It's the third time...

00:02:28.670 --> 00:02:30.750
...that Mai caused a problem.

00:02:30.920 --> 00:02:32.380
Sayuri-san.

00:02:37.130 --> 00:02:41.510
If she didn't do it, she should just say that she didn't, but...

00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:45.600
...since Mai's personality is like that, she doesn't say anything...

00:02:46.310 --> 00:02:47.730
There's no way she can say it.

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:52.270
That an invisible monster was the one that broke the glass...

00:02:53.110 --> 00:02:56.200
There's no way anyone would believe that if they were told...

00:02:57.570 --> 00:03:01.120
So, the student council keeps an eye on Mai.

00:03:01.330 --> 00:03:04.160
And when something happens, she gets summoned...

00:03:04.330 --> 00:03:07.120
Mai never argues back,

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:10.710
so she just gets lectured and punished...

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:12.000
"Punished"?

00:03:12.250 --> 00:03:14.590
Last time, it was detention...

00:03:17.260 --> 00:03:17.930
Mai...

00:03:18.050 --> 00:03:20.300
Surely, it's not detention...!?

00:03:20.930 --> 00:03:22.050
It's nothing...

00:03:22.430 --> 00:03:24.060
I just got scolded.

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:26.890
Class will start soon.

00:03:27.730 --> 00:03:29.980
Go back to your class right now.

00:03:30.770 --> 00:03:32.560
You're right, let's go.

00:03:34.070 --> 00:03:35.070
Kurata-san.

00:03:35.230 --> 00:03:37.950
You shouldn't be associating with a person like that.

00:03:38.610 --> 00:03:41.370
I believe Mai about this...

00:03:55.210 --> 00:03:56.420
That makes me angry!

00:03:56.590 --> 00:03:57.760
You've gone mad.

00:03:58.010 --> 00:03:59.420
I WILL be mad!

00:03:59.550 --> 00:04:04.010
That Kuze guy said, "You shouldn't be associating with a person like that"!

00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:06.270
What the hell is he thinking about other people!?

00:04:06.430 --> 00:04:08.020
I warned you as well.

00:04:08.270 --> 00:04:11.520
That you shouldn't get near Kawasumi Mai.

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:14.190
It's not like that.

00:04:14.310 --> 00:04:17.990
When you're irritable, it's proof that you're hungry.

00:04:18.780 --> 00:04:22.200
There's a good curry house at the shopping mall.

00:04:22.410 --> 00:04:23.950
Want to go with me?

00:04:24.200 --> 00:04:25.410
Curry?

00:04:25.910 --> 00:04:28.750
The owner is from India.

00:04:28.870 --> 00:04:31.540
I don't mind what it is.

00:04:31.580 --> 00:04:33.330
But Nayuki, what about club activities?

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:35.960
We don't have any today.

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:39.510
Okay, then wait at the gate.

00:04:39.920 --> 00:04:42.800
Yeah, I'll be waiting.

00:04:43.090 --> 00:04:43.800
Yeah...

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:46.430
You guys have a good relationship.

00:04:46.510 --> 00:04:49.600
Don't say something like that just because we're eating together.

00:04:53.270 --> 00:04:54.310
Yuuichi-san.

00:04:55.440 --> 00:04:56.480
Shiori.

00:05:01.530 --> 00:05:05.570
Um, thank you very much for yesterday.

00:05:05.910 --> 00:05:07.870
Give that thanks to Mai.

00:05:08.410 --> 00:05:09.580
"Mai"-san?

00:05:09.870 --> 00:05:12.120
The person who scared the dog away?

00:05:12.620 --> 00:05:13.330
Yup.

00:05:13.420 --> 00:05:15.630
She's an eccentric person though.

00:05:15.710 --> 00:05:17.710
She's wonderful.

00:05:18.960 --> 00:05:20.630
As if she's like a prince.

00:05:20.760 --> 00:05:22.220
A prince!?

00:05:22.340 --> 00:05:24.680
A prince that saves a girl in a pinch.

00:05:24.890 --> 00:05:28.600
Don't you think love will bloom from a situation like that?

00:05:30.060 --> 00:05:31.730
Don't laugh!

00:05:32.140 --> 00:05:34.810
There's no drama like that right now.

00:05:35.150 --> 00:05:37.360
First of all, Mai is a girl.

00:05:37.690 --> 00:05:39.360
You're right.

00:05:40.360 --> 00:05:42.150
But I yearn for it.

00:05:42.280 --> 00:05:44.610
Those drama like encounters.

00:05:45.450 --> 00:05:47.490
Oh yeah, you still didn't eat your lunch, right?

00:05:47.620 --> 00:05:49.410
If it's okay, do you want to come too?

00:05:49.490 --> 00:05:50.490
It's a curry house.

00:05:50.660 --> 00:05:53.000
Um, I can't eat spicy foods...

00:05:53.250 --> 00:05:54.290
You're still a kid.

00:05:54.410 --> 00:05:56.120
I hate it when people say that!

00:05:56.170 --> 00:05:58.130
Then what can you eat?

00:05:59.540 --> 00:06:01.340
Something like ice cream.

00:06:05.760 --> 00:06:09.260
"Ice cream"... The cold kind?

00:06:10.640 --> 00:06:12.770
Are there any warm kinds?

00:06:18.230 --> 00:06:20.610
Um, okay, wait a second.

00:06:22.690 --> 00:06:23.740
Is it good?

00:06:24.570 --> 00:06:27.450
Yes, it's my favorite. Vanilla ice cream.

00:06:27.780 --> 00:06:29.530
Would you like to eat some too, Yuuichi-san?

00:06:30.830 --> 00:06:32.200
I'll pass.

00:06:32.450 --> 00:06:33.620
Is it okay?

00:06:33.790 --> 00:06:34.960
That's too bad.

00:06:36.870 --> 00:06:38.420
I can't believe it.

00:06:39.330 --> 00:06:41.710
Is it bad to eat ice cream in the middle of winter?

00:06:41.960 --> 00:06:43.460
Um, it's not like that.

00:06:43.590 --> 00:06:48.050
Seeing you like this, I can't imagine you having a cold and being absent from school.

00:06:50.350 --> 00:06:53.770
By the way, isn't Yuuichi-san going to eat lunch?

00:06:54.020 --> 00:06:56.940
Oh no! Nayuki is still waiting for me at the gate!

00:06:57.020 --> 00:06:58.600
Shiori, see you later.

00:06:59.560 --> 00:07:01.230
I'm in trouble, I'm in trouble.

00:07:11.830 --> 00:07:13.290
Oh man!

00:07:16.830 --> 00:07:18.000
Liar.

00:07:18.420 --> 00:07:19.500
I'm sorry!

00:07:20.380 --> 00:07:25.340
You didn't come, so I thought you went ahead of me.

00:07:25.550 --> 00:07:28.300
I went to the curry house but you weren't there either,

00:07:28.720 --> 00:07:30.760
so I thought you went home ahead of me.

00:07:30.800 --> 00:07:34.100
I bought some nikuman and went home, but I saw that you still weren't home.
(T/L Note: Nikuman is a steamed meat bun.)

00:07:34.310 --> 00:07:36.060
I said I'm sorry!

00:07:36.100 --> 00:07:38.560
As an apology, I'll do whatever you say!

00:07:38.730 --> 00:07:39.730
Really?

00:07:39.730 --> 00:07:40.730
Yeah.

00:07:41.310 --> 00:07:44.940
Since tomorrow is Sunday, can you come shopping with me?

00:07:46.190 --> 00:07:47.990
I'll come too!

00:07:48.950 --> 00:07:50.700
"I'll come too!"...?

00:07:50.950 --> 00:07:53.740
Didn't you say that you had a grudge against me?

00:07:53.870 --> 00:07:56.080
It's a truce in the afternoon.

00:07:57.080 --> 00:07:58.710
What the hell is that?

00:07:59.540 --> 00:08:01.790
I don't care, but give my manga back.

00:08:02.920 --> 00:08:05.170
If you want to read, buy your own.

00:08:05.340 --> 00:08:06.920
You have money right?

00:08:07.550 --> 00:08:09.380
Can I buy manga too?

00:08:10.300 --> 00:08:11.840
Of course you can buy it.

00:08:13.050 --> 00:08:14.350
Can I buy this too?

00:08:16.140 --> 00:08:18.530
You can buy it, if you go to the shopping center.

00:08:19.060 --> 00:08:20.440
I see.

00:08:34.030 --> 00:08:35.330
Hey Yuuichi!

00:08:35.410 --> 00:08:39.080
It's mean to eat without telling me!

00:08:39.160 --> 00:08:40.660
What are you talking about...

00:08:40.790 --> 00:08:42.580
...after coming down this late.

00:08:42.920 --> 00:08:44.380
We called you many times.

00:08:44.420 --> 00:08:46.380
Like "The meal is ready!"

00:08:47.130 --> 00:08:48.550
I didn't hear it!

00:08:48.670 --> 00:08:51.050
You were completely absorbed in the manga, so you just didn't notice.

00:08:51.260 --> 00:08:54.590
If you want to eat something, just microwave it from the fridge.

00:08:54.800 --> 00:08:57.640
Since it was your mistake, don't trouble Akiko-san.

00:08:58.850 --> 00:09:01.020
Geez, Yuuichi's an idiot!

00:09:30.960 --> 00:09:32.420
So you were here.

00:09:34.340 --> 00:09:35.800
It's the same today as yesterday.

00:09:35.930 --> 00:09:38.430
Won't it be bad if the night watchman finds you?

00:09:40.140 --> 00:09:41.390
What is it?

00:09:41.730 --> 00:09:44.730
Well, you see, I'm some sort of accomplice.

00:09:46.020 --> 00:09:47.310
Wanna eat?

00:09:51.280 --> 00:09:53.780
Hey, Mai, what was that monster?

00:09:54.200 --> 00:09:55.570
Is there more than one?

00:09:56.990 --> 00:09:58.450
Why are you fighting?

00:09:58.620 --> 00:10:00.040
Were you asked to do it?

00:10:03.540 --> 00:10:05.750
Don't sit there all quiet, say something!

00:10:05.830 --> 00:10:08.630
Recently, the monsters have been stirring.

00:10:09.540 --> 00:10:13.800
Until I defeat all the monsters, I can't leave here.

00:10:15.130 --> 00:10:16.680
What do you mean by that?

00:10:17.470 --> 00:10:18.720
Wh-What is it!?

00:10:22.890 --> 00:10:24.390
Did the monsters appear!?

00:10:24.730 --> 00:10:27.190
Hey! This is not the time to eat!

00:10:27.350 --> 00:10:28.150
Mai!

00:10:28.400 --> 00:10:28.980
It's alright.

00:10:29.150 --> 00:10:31.690
I'm a ghost!!!

00:10:37.160 --> 00:10:38.700
Ouchhhh.

00:10:38.910 --> 00:10:40.240
What are you doing to me!?

00:10:40.240 --> 00:10:41.910
That's my line!

00:10:42.120 --> 00:10:43.870
What are you doing here!?

00:10:44.370 --> 00:10:46.160
Who cares about that!

00:10:46.210 --> 00:10:48.750
Auu... I got a bump.

00:10:48.790 --> 00:10:49.920
There, there.

00:10:49.960 --> 00:10:51.960
Hey, are you making fun of me?

00:10:52.090 --> 00:10:53.800
I thought you wanted me to do this.

00:10:54.340 --> 00:10:57.340
What is she! She's dangerous!

00:10:58.090 --> 00:11:00.470
Don't you say that when you tried to surprise us.

00:11:02.470 --> 00:11:04.350
Hey, is someone there?

00:11:04.470 --> 00:11:06.060
Damn! Let's run!

00:11:07.270 --> 00:11:08.650
Hey! What are you guys doing over there!?

00:11:14.320 --> 00:11:15.400
Wait!

00:11:23.620 --> 00:11:24.950
That was scary.

00:11:25.370 --> 00:11:26.660
Whose fault was it?

00:11:26.790 --> 00:11:28.870
Mai, go home for today.

00:11:29.000 --> 00:11:31.290
Maybe there are days that the monsters don't appear.

00:11:32.920 --> 00:11:33.920
But...

00:11:35.340 --> 00:11:36.880
The mentai onigiri...
(T/L Note: Mentai onigiri = cod roe riceball.)

00:11:36.880 --> 00:11:37.130
(T/L Note: Mentai onigiri = cod roe riceball.)

00:11:37.130 --> 00:11:38.430
That!?
(T/L Note: Mentai onigiri = cod roe riceball.)

00:11:39.760 --> 00:11:41.300
And the kanimayo onigiri too.
(T/L Note: kanimayo onigiri = crab meat with mayonnaise riceball.)

00:11:41.300 --> 00:11:43.010
(T/L Note: kanimayo onigiri = crab meat with mayonnaise riceball.)

00:11:43.010 --> 00:11:44.930
I'll buy them next time.

00:11:46.640 --> 00:11:47.390
Are you sure?

00:11:47.850 --> 00:11:48.890
Yeah.

00:11:49.560 --> 00:11:51.310
Okay, go straight home.

00:11:51.900 --> 00:11:53.980
Ah! Wait for me!

00:11:54.440 --> 00:11:57.240
Hey, hey, buy me some onigiri too.

00:11:57.280 --> 00:11:58.860
Use your own money to buy them.

00:11:59.070 --> 00:12:00.530
You have some, right?

00:12:12.160 --> 00:12:13.580
I'm leaving.

00:12:13.960 --> 00:12:15.380
Come back safely.

00:12:27.220 --> 00:12:28.430
(T/L Note: Neko = cat.)
It's a Neko-san!

00:12:32.310 --> 00:12:34.770
Hey, cut it out. Stray cats are pretty common now days.

00:12:34.980 --> 00:12:36.980
But they're cute.

00:12:37.360 --> 00:12:39.980
Neko, neko, neko, neko!

00:12:40.150 --> 00:12:41.360
Come here.

00:12:42.690 --> 00:12:44.240
Isn't it cute.

00:12:44.400 --> 00:12:46.490
Will it let me touch it?

00:12:46.610 --> 00:12:49.620
I want to stroke it and hug it.

00:12:53.410 --> 00:12:54.080
Don't do it.

00:12:54.210 --> 00:12:55.920
Your cat allergy will act up again.

00:12:57.080 --> 00:13:00.170
Your tears wouldn't stop when you touched one before.

00:13:00.420 --> 00:13:01.960
You remembered.

00:13:02.380 --> 00:13:05.130
I'd say "I just remembered it" instead of "I remembered it".

00:13:05.930 --> 00:13:07.680
Hey, isn't it okay?

00:13:07.800 --> 00:13:11.140
Isn't it okay to raise this Neko-san?

00:13:11.560 --> 00:13:14.930
Nayuki, I'll go find the owner.

00:13:15.230 --> 00:13:16.060
No!

00:13:16.310 --> 00:13:18.270
I'm going to raise this Neko-san!

00:13:18.350 --> 00:13:21.070
I like Neko-san!

00:13:25.740 --> 00:13:28.240
Hey Yuuichi, do you remember?

00:13:28.490 --> 00:13:34.790
That time, you said "I'll make a medicine for the cat allergy!" to me.

00:13:35.660 --> 00:13:37.920
Eh? Did I say that?

00:13:38.790 --> 00:13:39.710
Yes, you did!

00:13:39.830 --> 00:13:42.550
I'm not smart enough to be a doctor.

00:13:43.210 --> 00:13:44.590
"Fight!"

00:13:45.090 --> 00:13:48.840
You know, there are things that won't be rewarded even with effort.

00:13:51.850 --> 00:13:54.930
From now on, maybe you will remember more things.

00:13:55.060 --> 00:13:56.060
About the past.

00:13:56.810 --> 00:13:57.890
Yeah.

00:14:00.060 --> 00:14:05.240
Maybe Nayuki is right. I'm remembering bit by bit...

00:14:06.610 --> 00:14:09.780
...about the time I spent in this town when I was a kid.

00:14:11.570 --> 00:14:13.280
Huh, isn't that Makoto?

00:14:15.870 --> 00:14:18.160
Hey, what are you doing, Makoto?

00:14:20.080 --> 00:14:22.540
Why did you leave without me!?

00:14:22.920 --> 00:14:25.000
Who was the one sleeping and snoring?

00:14:25.590 --> 00:14:27.050
Huh? Shopping?

00:14:27.380 --> 00:14:28.930
Hm? Yup.

00:14:29.590 --> 00:14:30.760
Were you really able to buy stuff?

00:14:30.890 --> 00:14:32.100
Yes, I was!

00:14:32.140 --> 00:14:33.510
Since I'm an adult!

00:14:34.140 --> 00:14:35.470
"Adult", huh?

00:14:35.640 --> 00:14:35.970
Matsusaka Bookstore

00:14:35.970 --> 00:14:37.310
Hmmm, then...
Matsusaka Bookstore

00:14:37.310 --> 00:14:37.390
Matsusaka Bookstore

00:14:37.390 --> 00:14:38.100
Can I ask you to do my shopping?
Matsusaka Bookstore

00:14:38.100 --> 00:14:40.690
Can I ask you to do my shopping?

00:14:44.980 --> 00:14:47.240
I got it! I'll go buy it!

00:14:47.400 --> 00:14:48.610
Seriously?

00:14:48.820 --> 00:14:50.820
Don't worry, leave it to me.

00:14:52.490 --> 00:14:55.700
If you don't know where it is, ask the clerk.

00:14:55.790 --> 00:14:57.660
The ones they recommend are fine.

00:14:57.790 --> 00:14:58.870
Okay!

00:15:02.210 --> 00:15:04.120
Hey, what did you ask for?

00:15:04.290 --> 00:15:05.420
Just watch.

00:15:05.420 --> 00:15:08.130
Books

00:15:08.130 --> 00:15:09.130
Excuse me...
Books

00:15:09.130 --> 00:15:09.970
Books

00:15:09.970 --> 00:15:10.380
Yes?
Books

00:15:10.380 --> 00:15:10.840
Yes?

00:15:12.430 --> 00:15:14.510
Where are your erotic books?

00:15:14.930 --> 00:15:15.930
Huh!?

00:15:16.010 --> 00:15:17.180
Please give me some erotic books!

00:15:17.220 --> 00:15:18.430
Any of the ones you would recommend.

00:15:18.980 --> 00:15:20.730
That idiot! Not so loud!

00:15:21.440 --> 00:15:23.020
Makoto! Hurry, this way!

00:15:27.440 --> 00:15:29.820
I thought my face was going to catch fire!

00:15:30.450 --> 00:15:34.320
I didn't think that you would seriously try to buy it.

00:15:35.030 --> 00:15:36.910
Eh? What do you mean?

00:15:37.160 --> 00:15:40.580
Um, what Yuuichi tried to make you buy was...

00:15:41.870 --> 00:15:43.920
Geez! You're the worst!

00:15:44.130 --> 00:15:46.960
Because you were insisting on saying that you're an adult.

00:15:47.090 --> 00:15:49.880
Girls don't buy those kinds of books even if they're adults!

00:15:49.960 --> 00:15:50.090
You idiot!

00:15:50.090 --> 00:15:51.220
Oh, Makoto!
You idiot!

00:15:51.220 --> 00:15:51.470
Oh, Makoto!

00:15:53.010 --> 00:15:54.680
Yuuichi's the one at fault.

00:16:02.560 --> 00:16:05.730
On a night like this, she surely didn't go out defeating the monsters, did she?

00:16:09.690 --> 00:16:11.320
The bath is ready.

00:16:11.860 --> 00:16:12.780
Oh.

00:16:14.070 --> 00:16:18.450
That girl, she would be charming if she were always like that.

00:16:21.830 --> 00:16:23.160
What's that smell?

00:16:23.500 --> 00:16:25.420
Did she put in some bath salts?

00:16:26.500 --> 00:16:28.960
But that can't be it, this smell is...

00:16:32.420 --> 00:16:34.380
MAKOTOOOOOO!!!

00:16:34.470 --> 00:16:36.470
What? What? What happened?

00:16:37.220 --> 00:16:40.220
Oh! The bath turned into miso soup!

00:16:40.470 --> 00:16:44.140
How can YOU tell if you didn't go into it!!

00:16:44.350 --> 00:16:47.900
You didn't put an entire bagful in there, did you?

00:16:48.150 --> 00:16:50.110
We'll be fine for the next month now.

00:16:50.780 --> 00:16:53.360
We're going to drink this? From here?

00:16:53.650 --> 00:16:54.780
It's a joke.

00:16:56.110 --> 00:16:59.080
Makoto, you shouldn't waste food.

00:16:59.280 --> 00:17:00.030
Yes!

00:17:00.870 --> 00:17:01.910
She's not apologizing.

00:17:01.910 --> 00:17:04.040
She's DEFINITELY not apologizing.

00:17:13.260 --> 00:17:15.260
Now what's the fuss about this time?

00:17:17.220 --> 00:17:18.640
They're fireworks.

00:17:18.850 --> 00:17:22.850
Geez, playing with fireworks at night. What a nuisance to the neighbors.

00:17:23.220 --> 00:17:24.140
I...!

00:17:24.770 --> 00:17:27.730
Hey you, what's that in your hand?

00:17:28.060 --> 00:17:28.730
Auu!

00:17:29.730 --> 00:17:31.770
Did you want to play with fireworks?

00:17:32.030 --> 00:17:33.070
Auu...

00:17:33.610 --> 00:17:35.490
Fireworks are something that you play with outside.

00:17:35.860 --> 00:17:38.070
When it's warmer, let's do it with everyone.

00:17:39.620 --> 00:17:40.580
Yes.

00:17:41.450 --> 00:17:44.580
Okay, it's late right now, so everyone get to sleep.

00:17:45.000 --> 00:17:46.210
Yes.

00:17:47.620 --> 00:17:48.500
You!

00:17:48.920 --> 00:17:50.170
Damn!

00:17:54.380 --> 00:17:56.470
Good morning.

00:17:56.920 --> 00:17:58.630
Good morning, Yuuichi...

00:17:59.640 --> 00:18:00.340
Good morning.

00:18:00.390 --> 00:18:01.470
You're up early.

00:18:01.930 --> 00:18:03.220
And Makoto too.

00:18:03.680 --> 00:18:04.970
Good morning, Yuuichi-kun!

00:18:05.730 --> 00:18:07.640
Hey you! What are you doing here?

00:18:07.730 --> 00:18:08.480
Eating breakfast.

00:18:08.560 --> 00:18:09.810
I can tell just by looking.

00:18:10.060 --> 00:18:13.980
When I was taking out the trash, I met Ayu-chan by chance, so...

00:18:13.980 --> 00:18:16.940
...I asked her if she wanted to eat breakfast with us.

00:18:17.360 --> 00:18:20.780
Don't ask her just because you met her on the street.

00:18:20.910 --> 00:18:22.450
I think it's okay.

00:18:22.620 --> 00:18:23.990
Even if it's okay for you...

00:18:24.080 --> 00:18:26.040
I think it's okay too.

00:18:26.250 --> 00:18:27.330
Right?

00:18:28.290 --> 00:18:30.460
When did they start getting along so well?

00:18:32.460 --> 00:18:34.000
Thanks for the meal.

00:18:34.340 --> 00:18:35.710
I'm glad you enjoyed it.

00:18:36.420 --> 00:18:37.630
Then, let's go.

00:18:37.760 --> 00:18:38.090
Yup!

00:18:38.510 --> 00:18:39.930
Good morning...

00:18:42.890 --> 00:18:44.390
What do you mean, "Good morning"?

00:18:44.560 --> 00:18:47.850
You eat, sleep, and read manga. What a great school you go to, geez.

00:18:48.140 --> 00:18:50.350
Yuuichi! That's saying too much!

00:18:56.190 --> 00:18:57.740
Hey, Yuuichi-kun.

00:18:59.860 --> 00:19:01.490
Go home, Makoto!

00:19:10.040 --> 00:19:11.750
I told you to go home!

00:19:12.000 --> 00:19:13.460
That's so mean!

00:19:13.540 --> 00:19:15.880
You don't know anything about her!

00:19:16.170 --> 00:19:18.970
If she gets into an accident, it'll be Yuuichi-kun's fault!

00:19:19.340 --> 00:19:22.890
Even though you said to go home, maybe she can't get back alone.

00:19:23.930 --> 00:19:25.970
Damn, fine!

00:19:26.220 --> 00:19:28.560
I'll take her, take care of roll call at school for me.

00:19:28.890 --> 00:19:30.060
I can't do that!

00:19:30.060 --> 00:19:31.440
Use guts! Guts!

00:19:32.230 --> 00:19:35.520
Geez, what are you thinking?

00:19:36.940 --> 00:19:38.820
Now I'm definitely going to be late.

00:19:39.530 --> 00:19:41.780
But I hate being alone.

00:19:42.070 --> 00:19:44.450
Akiko-san also goes to work...

00:19:44.620 --> 00:19:45.910
In the house, I'm all alo...

00:19:45.910 --> 00:19:47.370
Ah! What is it?

00:19:47.830 --> 00:19:50.040
This little guy is the cat from yesterday.

00:19:50.580 --> 00:19:52.040
Is he hungry?

00:19:54.500 --> 00:19:55.590
Is it good?

00:19:55.790 --> 00:19:57.590
It seems that you're all alone too.

00:19:57.800 --> 00:20:00.760
Being alone without anywhere to go to...

00:20:02.840 --> 00:20:04.760
Why don't we raise this little guy at home?

00:20:06.100 --> 00:20:07.810
He's taken a liking to you anyway.

00:20:08.260 --> 00:20:10.680
Akiko-san will give us the okay in no time.

00:20:11.180 --> 00:20:14.190
It will be difficult for Nayuki, but as long as she doesn't go near it...

00:20:15.560 --> 00:20:17.320
That's too pitiful...

00:20:18.270 --> 00:20:19.230
"Pitiful"?

00:20:21.650 --> 00:20:25.110
When he's taken in, he might be truly happy for a while,

00:20:25.240 --> 00:20:27.030
but he's going to be far more miserable when he's eventually abandoned again.

00:20:27.910 --> 00:20:31.500
He will miss the warm futons and the delicious meals,

00:20:31.500 --> 00:20:33.750
and become sorrowful, and die.

00:20:34.370 --> 00:20:37.170
This stray cat should remain a stray.

00:20:38.130 --> 00:20:39.630
That's not a stray.

00:20:39.960 --> 00:20:41.800
It could be dangerous to leave it loose.

00:20:42.800 --> 00:20:44.720
You should take care of it.

00:20:45.680 --> 00:20:50.430
Animals are... always thrown away when they are no longer wanted, that's their fate.

00:20:52.390 --> 00:20:54.440
Idiot, stop it!

00:20:54.640 --> 00:20:55.310
Ouch!

00:21:02.320 --> 00:21:04.200
What the hell are you doing!?

00:21:04.280 --> 00:21:05.610
It's Yuuichi's fault!

00:21:05.740 --> 00:21:09.200
Because Yuuichi tried to take away the cat...

00:21:17.830 --> 00:21:20.800
Yuuichi's an IDIOT!!

00:21:30.050 --> 00:21:31.010
I'm home.

00:21:31.390 --> 00:21:32.600
Welcome home.

00:21:51.280 --> 00:21:52.700
Akiko-san, where's Makoto?

00:21:53.580 --> 00:21:54.580
Don't know.

00:21:54.870 --> 00:21:57.620
It seems that she came home and went out again.

00:21:58.170 --> 00:21:59.420
Did something happen?

00:22:00.960 --> 00:22:02.800
At that time, my intuition told me...

00:22:03.460 --> 00:22:05.010
That she wouldn't be back...

00:22:06.090 --> 00:22:07.300
But, where'd she go to...?

00:22:08.590 --> 00:22:11.680
Is there even a place for her to go home to?

00:22:25.270 --> 00:22:30.170
In between the flowing clouds
nagareru kunono aimani

00:22:30.530 --> 00:22:35.910
The crawling blue sky
muzuita aozora ga

00:22:36.530 --> 00:22:41.590
Even causes the familiar town
minareta machinami de sae

00:22:41.850 --> 00:22:47.060
To light up
kagayakasete kureru

00:22:47.840 --> 00:22:52.900
Running small back
kaketeku chiisana senaka

00:22:53.160 --> 00:22:58.790
The two at that time were...
anokoro no futariga

00:22:59.200 --> 00:23:04.210
The reason for the spilling pain
koboreru itami no wakewo

00:23:04.470 --> 00:23:09.950
Hidden with innocence
mujyakisa de kakushita

00:23:12.580 --> 00:23:18.320
Time is flowing quietly
tokiwa shizukani nagare

00:23:18.630 --> 00:23:23.950
The gentle winds blow
yasashii kaze ga fuita

00:23:24.200 --> 00:23:29.580
Numbed feelings too will
Kajikanda omoimo

00:23:29.830 --> 00:23:35.830
Change to a smile
egao ni kawarukara

